><span><span>You are working in repo https://github.com/tyomakr/SpringWebPa=
rser in branch rewrite/akcp.
Goal: greenfield rewrite into =E2=80=9CAK Content Pipeline (AKCP)=E2=80=9D =
while keeping git history (DO NOT create a new repo).
IMPORTANT RULES:
- DO NOT run `git commit`, do not create commits, do not push. Leave change=
s unstaged unless explicitly asked later.
- Do not introduce unnecessary infrastructure or extra services.
- Keep everything buildable and testable at each step.
- Never add real secrets/tokens to the repository. Use env vars and .env.ex=
ample only.

HIGH-LEVEL PRODUCT CONCEPT
AKCP is a personal content pipeline: ingest content from sources (web parse=
r, Telegram later, VK wall syncing later), store in a unified library (chro=
nological feed with tags), and publish selected items to targets (VK initia=
lly; Telegram target later). AI recommendation is a later phase, but archit=
ecture must reserve a place for it, including optional remote GPU =E2=80=9C=
accelerator node=E2=80=9D.

TECH STACK &amp; CONSTRAINTS
- Backend: Java 21, Spring Boot 3.x, WebFlux (reactive), Maven multi-module=
, OpenAPI/Swagger UI.
- DB: PostgreSQL as default. Use Flyway migrations. Prepare for pgvector (o=
ptional extension) later, but do NOT require it for MVP.
- Auth: JWT (stateless), role-based: ADMIN, MODERATOR, AGENT.
- Containers: docker-compose with separate services for backend, db, and (l=
ater) frontend. For now provide frontend skeleton + container wiring, but M=
VP focus is backend.
- Secrets: only via environment variables or mounted files outside git. Pro=
vide `.env.example` (never commit `.env`).
- Documentation: Keep `/docs/*.md` updated. Also keep OpenAPI as living API=
 contract.

BRANCH RESET / CLEANUP REQUIREMENT
In this branch, remove old application code and create a clean structure. K=
eep only:
- README.md (rewrite to AKCP)
- LICENSE (if exists)
- .gitignore
- optionally a root-level `docs/` folder (new)
Everything else may be removed or moved into an `legacy/` folder ONLY if st=
rictly needed (prefer removal in this branch; history preserves it anyway).

PROJECT STRUCTURE (CREATE NEW)
Create a Maven multi-module project at repository root:
- pom.xml (parent)
- backend/ (aggregator module or root for backend modules)
  - backend/pom.xml (backend parent)
  - backend/akcp-app (Spring Boot runnable app; depends on other modules)
  - backend/akcp-core (domain model, interfaces, shared utils)
  - backend/akcp-library (feed, tags, storage services)
  - backend/akcp-ingestion-web (manual web parsing module; MVP uses this)
  - backend/akcp-publishing-vk (publishing target to VK; MVP can be stubbed=
)
  - backend/akcp-auth (JWT, security)
  - backend/akcp-jobs (job/task framework; scheduling, processing pipeline =
skeleton)
- ui/ (React app skeleton; keep minimal, ensure docker build works, but do =
not implement full UI now)
- docker/ (compose files, db init if needed)
- docs/ (architecture.md, modules.md, security.md, deployment.md, api.md)

MVP SCOPE (PHASE 1)
Implement a minimal, working backend with:
1) Hello endpoint + health endpoint.
2) DB migrations via Flyway.
3) Core domain: Item, Attachment, Tag, SourceRef, PublishTarget, Job.
4) Library endpoints:
   - Create Item manually (POST /api/items)
   - List Items (GET /api/items?cursor=3D&amp;limit=3D&amp;from=3D&amp;to=
=3D&amp;tag=3D) =E2=80=94 cursor-based pagination preferred.
   - Add/remove tags to Item (PATCH)
   - Get single Item by id
5) Ingestion-web (manual): provide an endpoint to submit a URL and parse im=
age links with a simple heuristic (do NOT overcomplicate). Store discovered=
 images as Attachments and create Items.
   - POST /api/ingestion/web/parse { url } -&gt; returns parsed candidate a=
ttachments and optionally creates items (choose a simple flow and document =
it).
6) Publishing-vk: for MVP create an interface + stub implementation and end=
points that queue a publish job (do not require real VK token in tests).
   - POST /api/publish/vk/{itemId} -&gt; creates PublishJob in DB with stat=
us QUEUED.
7) Jobs: simple job runner skeleton that can pick queued jobs periodically =
(Spring scheduler) and mark them DONE/FAILED. For now VK job execution can =
be stubbed (no real HTTP calls unless token is provided).
8) OpenAPI: swagger-ui enabled in dev.
9) Tests:
   - Unit tests for domain/service layers.
   - Integration test using Testcontainers for PostgreSQL verifying Flyway =
+ basic CRUD + pagination.
10) Docker compose:
   - `docker-compose.yml` with db and backend.
   - Provide `.env.example` with required vars.

SECURITY REQUIREMENTS
- JWT auth enabled. Minimal auth flow for MVP:
  - Provide a dev-only user in env vars: AKCP_ADMIN_USERNAME / AKCP_ADMIN_P=
ASSWORD (or generate a single admin in migration).
  - Provide /api/auth/login that returns JWT.
  - Secure all /api/** except /actuator/health (or /health).
- Document in docs/security.md how to configure secrets.

AI / RECOMMENDATION PLACEHOLDERS (NO FULL IMPLEMENTATION NOW)
Reserve interfaces and minimal schema fields without implementing heavy mod=
els:
- Interface `EmbeddingProvider` with modes:
  - LOCAL (CPU) placeholder
  - REMOTE (calls remote worker URL) placeholder
- Config properties:
  - akcp.ai.mode=3Dlocal|remote
  - akcp.ai.remote.url
- Add Job types: COMPUTE_PHASH, COMPUTE_EMBEDDING, PUBLISH_VK
- Mention in docs/ai-design.md the future plan:
  - pHash dedup
  - embeddings via DJL+ONNX
  - optional remote GPU worker node
Do NOT add DJL dependencies yet unless necessary; keep placeholders.

SECRETS &amp; CONFIG
- Use Spring config with `${ENV_VAR:default}` pattern.
- Create `.env.example` with:
  - POSTGRES_DB, POSTGRES_USER, POSTGRES_PASSWORD
  - AKCP_JWT_SECRET
  - AKCP_ADMIN_USERNAME, AKCP_ADMIN_PASSWORD
  - optional VK_* (placeholders only)
- Ensure `.env` is in .gitignore.

DOCUMENTATION
Create docs:
- docs/architecture.md: domains, modules, data flow
- docs/modules.md: responsibilities and boundaries
- docs/security.md: JWT + secrets management + no tokens in repo
- docs/deployment.md: docker compose runbook
- docs/api.md: overview of endpoints + pagination contract
- docs/ai-design.md: placeholders, future GPU worker concept

IMPLEMENTATION DETAILS / QUALITY
- Use hexagonal-ish boundaries: controllers -&gt; services -&gt; repositori=
es.
- Use R2DBC for Postgres (reactive). If too complex for MVP tests, you may =
use JDBC + WebFlux (still ok), but prefer reactive stack if feasible.
- Keep code clean, minimal, readable. Avoid premature microservices.
- Provide consistent package naming, use `ru.tyomakr.akcp` (or similar) pac=
kages.
- Ensure `mvn test` passes.
- Update README.md to reflect AKCP, how to run locally with docker compose,=
 how to login and call APIs.

DELIVERABLES CHECKLIST
- New Maven multi-module structure
- Spring Boot app starts
- Flyway migrations apply
- CRUD endpoints for Items/Tags work
- Swagger UI works
- Basic auth/login returns JWT
- Docker compose runs db + backend
- Tests pass
- Docs exist

Now execute the refactor/creation in this branch accordingly. Show the fina=
l file tree summary and key commands to run locally (mvn test, docker compo=
se up).
Remember: DO NOT COMMIT.
